 fixture public-key pin; no-pin and unrelated-key cases reject TLS. This is explicit test
 key trust, not browser CA-chain validation or deployed worker-transport acceptance.
 No global trust store is modified, and no external/Oracle deployment is certified.
+
+Browser sign-in returns `429 SESSION_CAPACITY_REACHED` when another session would
+exceed the local credential operator's existing 32-entry recovery journal for that
+actor (normally one LOCAL credential plus at most 31 browser sessions). Sign out an
+existing session or rotate credentials with the OS operator to free capacity. A
+replacement sign-in can reuse its old session's slot; a failed replacement leaves
+the old session valid. Sign-in marks expired or orphaned browser sessions revoked
+and retains their history. Admission and rotation use the same transaction lock,
+so concurrent sign-ins cannot prevent the operator from rotating or revoking access.
